}
```

The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
if (READ_ONCE(msk->snd_data_fin_enable) && !(ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN)) {
    ...
    tcp_shutdown(ssk, SEND_SHUTDOWN);
}
```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the condition checks if the MPTCP socket is not in a shutdown state before attempting to shut down the TCP connection. If the MPTCP socket has already been shut down before this check, the TCP connection will not be closed, leading to resource leaks and undefined behavior.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
if (READ_ONCE(msk->snd_data_fin_enable) && !(ssk->sk_shutdown & SEND_SHUTDOWN)) {
    ...
    tcp_shutdown(ssk, SEND_SHUTDOWN);
}
```
Reason:
The fix explicitly checks for the critical condition of whether the MPTCP socket is in a shutdown state before proceeding with the TCP shutdown. This ensures that the TCP connection is properly closed if the MPTCP socket is shutting down, preventing the resource leak and ensuring the network stack behaves correctly.

